 ('frz7', "The paintings are what make Ajanta famous. Pigment on a prepared plaster ground, in a technique related to but not identical with true fresco. The subjects are largely Jataka stories — tales of the Buddha's previous lives — along with court scenes, animals, flowers and elaborate ceilings."),
 ('frz8', "Following this series' rule, we are showing the ornament and the borders rather than the figures. What you should carry away is that this is the best surviving body of ancient Indian painting, and nearly all of it is in caves."),
